course: dictionary
lesson: 5833
title: Words that fill you with wonder
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Majestic» means very grand, beautiful and impressive, like a king or queen. A majestic thing makes you stop and stare. Mountains, eagles, lions and old castles can all be majestic.
explain: In «The Wind in the Willows», the Mole says to Ratty, «You argued it out, step by step, in that wise head of yours... and at once your majestic mind said to itself, "Door-scraper!"» The clues are wise, argued and step by step. They show that Ratty's clever mind is impressive, so the Mole praises it as grand.
explain: Authors choose words like majestic to make us feel something. Saying a mountain is majestic tells us more than saying it is big. Ask yourself what the word makes you feel, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
fact: Majestic is an adjective: majestic, more majestic, most majestic.
fact: «Majestic» means very grand, beautiful and impressive, like a king or queen.
fact: «Majestic» often describes things that fill you with wonder, such as mountains, eagles, lions, ships and old buildings.
fact: Grand and stately are close in meaning to majestic, but majestic often suggests real beauty as well.
fact: In «your majestic mind», the Mole means Ratty's mind is wonderfully clever and impressive.
exercise: «The majestic eagle circled above the valley.» What does majestic mean here? | Very wet | Very hungry | *Very grand and impressive | Very small and quick
exercise: The Mole says Ratty has a «majestic mind». What is he saying? | Ratty is cross with the Mole | *Ratty's mind is clever and impressive | Ratty has a crown on his head | Ratty is tired and slow
exercise: Which thing would a child most likely call majestic? | A tiny pebble on the path | *A snow-capped mountain above the clouds | A soggy sock | A pencil with no point
test: Which word is closest in meaning to majestic? | Silly | Ordinary | Slippery | *Grand
test: «The lion walked across the grassland with majestic steps.» What does majestic tell you about the lion? | It was tired and sleepy | It was very small | It was lost and looking for its family | *It moved in a proud, impressive way
exam: The Mole calls Ratty's mind «majestic». Which best explains what majestic means? | Wet and muddy | *Very grand, beautiful and impressive, like a king or queen | Quick and noisy | Hungry and sad
